{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791886183,"nonce":"LNzcijZqKasSsbTOMtYrCGa8GCY=","title":"Reject stale queued numeric input synchronization","message":"During Move cancellation the editor restores exact authored values while Input.textual already has formatting queued for the previous numeric value. Its two directional Watch reactions can apply stale captured values, causing the text and numeric signals to oscillate indefinitely in LayoutTree.flush. An isolated Watch diagnostic reaches over 150 reads for the text-to-number synchronization watch; a native stack sample shows repeated regexp parsing and the process grows in memory. No simulation or runtime change is required.\n\nPrepared Input fix prioritizes external numeric writes, ignores stale text reactions and formats the current numeric value. An isolated source overlay passes Move drag/undo/redo/Escape/tool-switch checks in both themes. Focused reproducer: ChimpMonk repro/ashui_number_sync/Repro.hx, with bounded Watch draining; also check partial text, manual entry and latest parent writes. This supporting fix is necessary for the explicitly requested SceneKit/editor Move integration.","files":null}]}